   gts_eromanga.17.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with an action game titled §Y《Black-Fur Cat: Pulu》§! taking home the top prize. \nThis work imagines an alternate ending to the Battle of Heaven: After the legendary cat-girl warrior Apro led her forces to defeat the two Awakened Empires, she intended to retire and spend the rest of her life on an ordinary planet inhabited by Tiny persons. However, she was tragically betrayed by the Fourth Calamity; the Tiny persons she had raised were seized as playthings by other Giantess leaders, and Apro is beaten to death by her former comrade, Yanqi Repu. Players will take on the role of the Hakki—heirs to the Will of the Keycaps who emerge out of nowhere centuries later. To uncover the truth behind the “Supermarket Mystery” surrounding Apro, they will battle Giantess leaders of all sizes and ultimately fulfill their destiny to become the strongest and most ruthless Giantess."
   gts_eromanga.18.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a first-person shooter (FPS) game titled §Y《Field War 1》§! taking top honors. \nSet against the backdrop of the First Earth United Civil War, the game allows players to experience firsthand a series of conflicts and campaigns across Earth’s vast battlefronts between the two hegemonic blocs: the Entente and the Allies. To simulate an era of explosive military technological advancement—when giant mecha evolved from cutting-edge industrial marvels into mass-produced war machines—the game creatively introduces the “Giantess” mechanic. When one side falls behind, a Giantess arrives to provide support; these hundreds-of-meters-tall Giantesses can effortlessly tip the Libra of war: “Zeppelin” can crush the Graba Mountain Tunnel with a single stomp and grind most of a banquet hall to dust beneath her breasts with a single tumble; “Dreadnought” can ram through the century-old fortress of Faou, and shatter the coastal defenses of Zeebrugge; “Char” watches over the highlands of Soissons, and once corrupted, can level the supposedly impregnable Fort Faulx with a single kick; “Odin” and “Zamurets” rampage through the sandy deserts of the Middle East and the snowy plains of Eastern Europe. Yet the Giantesses of this era are not invincible; enemy soldiers can use various explosives and artillery to try to blow their outfits off, ultimately forcing them into a state of embarrassment and causing them to faint on the ground. \nThe First Earth United Civil War concluded with “Zeppelin” storming Paris and Britain’s conditional surrender, bringing thirty years of peace to the Allied Powers (later known as the Imperial Covenant). Thirty years later, the Imperial Covenant would face its second decisive battle against the Industrial Union in the West and the Lucia Alliance in the East."
   gts_eromanga.19.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most highly anticipated entertainment awards—have been announced, with a casual game titled §Y《Tales of Starlight Grains》§! taking home the top prize. \nAfter being laid off by the corporate giant Joja, players return to their hometown of Wenko Water, a Gaia-like planet meticulously transformed by horticultural automatons, to stay with their Giantess older sister, who runs a farm. In addition to farming and raising livestock in the bonsai garden their sister has prepared for them, players will also leverage their advantage as a Tiny person on this planet full of Giantesses, venturing into mines inaccessible to the Giantesses to explore, collect various ancient treasures, help the townspeople resist the Enterprise’s economic infiltration, interact with various Giantesses as the seasons change, and ultimately forge friendships or even marital relationships. \nThe game’s careful attention to mechanics, music, and atmosphere perfectly fulfills players’ fantasies of living in harmony with Giantesses in an idyllic pastoral setting, creating a virtual haven filled with warmth and the joy of exploration for the Tiny persons who are often toyed with by the Giantesses."
-  gts_eromanga.20.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a real-time strategy game titled §Y *Command & Conquer: Mind Omega* §! taking top honors. \nThis title serves as a narrative expansion of its predecessor, §Y《Command & Conquer: Yuri’s Revenge》§!, allowing players to experience a timeline entirely distinct from the original through a series of campaigns commanding three factions: Following the First Soviet-Moe War, the New Soviet Union—backed by the Moe Army—lay low with the help of Yuri, a yuri Giantess enthusiast, before launching a surprise attack that dealt a crushing blow to the Moe Army, sparking the Second Soviet-Moe War. As the war progressed, Yuri attempted to reap the benefits as a third party, and his conspiracy to establish a world ruled by Giantesses came to light, forcing the Soviet Union and the Moe Army to temporarily cooperate and jointly eliminate Yuri’s Epsilon Legion. \nAlthough the Soviet-Moe Alliance successfully recaptured most of the territory occupied by the Epsilon Legion, they failed to prevent Libra—a super-powered Giantess bred by Yuri—from activating the mind-control tower during the Antarctic Campaign. Ultimately, Libra took control of all human minds and grew into a 10,000-meter-tall Giantess, ushering in a new era for Earth’s civilization. \nThe only hope for ending this catastrophe rested with the newly formed Fengfeng faction. Through reverse engineering, Yunru—who had also grown into a 10,000-meter-tall Giantess—led exiled forces from various nations to establish a containment barrier at Cape Hope in Alaska, awaiting the opportunity to resist Libra."
\ No newline at end of file
+  gts_eromanga.20.desc: "The results of the Golden Dove Awards—the Empire’s most prestigious entertainment awards—have been announced, with a real-time strategy game titled §Y *Command & Conquer: Mind Omega* §! taking top honors. \nThis title serves as a narrative expansion of its predecessor, §Y《Command & Conquer: Yuri’s Revenge》§!, allowing players to experience a timeline entirely distinct from the original through a series of campaigns commanding three factions: Following the First Soviet-Moe War, the New Soviet Union—backed by the Moe Army—lay low with the help of Yuri, a yuri Giantess enthusiast, before launching a surprise attack that dealt a crushing blow to the Moe Army, sparking the Second Soviet-Moe War. As the war progressed, Yuri attempted to reap the benefits as a third party, and his conspiracy to establish a world ruled by Giantesses came to light, forcing the Soviet Union and the Moe Army to temporarily cooperate and jointly eliminate Yuri’s Epsilon Legion. \nAlthough the Soviet-Moe Alliance successfully recaptured most of the territory occupied by the Epsilon Legion, they failed to prevent Libra—a super-powered Giantess bred by Yuri—from activating the mind-control tower during the Antarctic Campaign. Ultimately, Libra took control of all human minds and grew into a 10,000-meter-tall Giantess, ushering in a new era for Earth’s civilization. \nThe only hope for ending this catastrophe rested with the newly formed Fengfeng faction. Through reverse engineering, Yunru—who had also grown into a 10,000-meter-tall Giantess—led exiled forces from various nations to establish a containment barrier at Cape Hope in Alaska, awaiting the opportunity to resist Libra."
